### E. The Buddha's middle way prevents the ending from becoming nihilism

This is the philosophical correction I would make to your current ending.

The argument isn't that nothing exists or that everything is a hallucination.

In the Kaccānagotta Sutta (SN 12.15), the Buddha explicitly rejects both the view that everything exists in an absolute sense and the view that everything does not exist.

Instead he teaches dependent arising.&#x20;

