## 8. A few further connections worth exploring

Nāgārjuna — what if even the answer is empty?

In Mūlamadhyamakakārikā 24.18, dependent arising, emptiness and conventional designation are closely connected. In Chapter 25, Nāgārjuna subjects nirvāṇa itself to analysis rather than permitting it to become an independently existing metaphysical prize. This would sharpen your idea about nirvāṇa not being a hidden destination discovered at the end of a journey. But don't conflate his Madhyamaka arguments with all early Buddhist positions.&#x20;

